**Definition 6.2 (selection given a represented history).** The following
algorithm implements the table, including partial records. All operations
are on acquired/derived representations, not live source or meter reads.

First traverse actual seed/local CAP origins, initial field order and
ingress creation chains by their distinct grammars. Resolve a referenced
span by Nth on the port, unary base cancellation and TakeItems; retain its raw
tracks, markers and actual complete origin. Follow a descriptor predecessor
only to a strictly earlier creation reference and deduplicate references
by Find. Enumerate finite selected slots by their catalog identities.
For complete input blocks use their actual descriptor length/status; for
the live incomplete block use its real PC/head/base/counter frontier as
in Definition 6.3. These basic scans do not need cover/package contents.

For construction roles fold the already derived finite native history in
row order. Maintain finite-word lists of open/closed typed spans and their
actual port positions. The static role directory consists of ARC's native
capture/initial-field, ingress, cover-record, package-record, sender-export,
mailbox/receiver-allocation, payload-copy, descriptor, seal, completion and
fault call sites, followed by the five new stage call sites. It is the
call-path/row numbering of Definition 2.3, obtained by the same syntactic
expansion as the captured code. The fixed distinguished-entry directory
uses that order; it is code metadata, not an unrecorded runtime choice.

On entering a listed construction span record its current actual destination
and Base-derived start. Whenever its Append/Zero EX changes an old R into
the next backing cell, add that **old R identity immediately**, even before
WR. Record subsequent writes, F/seal/descriptor and origin-copy relations
at their actual rows. The fresh trailing R is boundary context, not a
consumed input. During payload copies mark the actual initialized destination
span, preserving its local identity and the copied origin. At a completion
record close only that declared span. Snapshot the selected relations at
the stopping cut; an unfinished record remains its constructed prefix.

The 71 cover/package/sender/completion roles and 73 receiver roles enter
family 5; unrelated bank registers, scratch and failed-fault records do
not become callable objects. Stage publications use the same sender/
receiver roles, so their actual backing is included when selected. Family
1 stops at the declared immutable initial-prefix endpoint, or at its actual
partial frontier if earlier. The role directory comes from finite code
and literal call paths, not interpretation of an unsealed payload as a
valid object. Project the marked endpoint cells/slots/relations, sort and
serialize by Definition 6.1. No full history is emitted as a memory field.

